n call sites ... five in _mcp_llm.py ... eleven in _lib_ops.py (three LLM workflow ops ... plus eight NON-LLM bridge/reconciler-mapping ops) ... and one in _engine/rebar_reconciler/__main__.py'","Grep of _lib_ops.py shows exactly 10 _shadow( calls: lines 58,76,86 (run_workflow/get_workflow_status/get_workflow_result LLM) and 102,110,129,150,224,264,289 (7 bridge ops)","Grep of _mcp_llm.py shows 5; reconciler __main__.py shows 1 emit_shadow_snapshot(surface='reconciler')","5+10+1 = 16, and plan subtotals 5+11+1 = 17 contradict the stated 18"],"finding":"The plan's shadow call-site inventory does not match the repository: it claims EIGHTEEN sites with 'eleven in _lib_ops.py (three LLM workflow ops plus eight NON-LLM bridge/reconciler-mapping ops)', but _lib_ops.py actually contains 10 _shadow(...) sites (3 workflow LLM + 7 non-LLM bridge), giving 5 (_mcp_llm) + 10 (_lib_ops) + 1 (reconciler) = 16 total, not 18. The plan's own subtotals (5+11+1) also sum to 17, not 18.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f4f6b97f7e2aa7299","impact":0.85,"is_primary":null,"location":"Context/Problem paragraph 3 and 'Call-site classification' / Scope bullet for _lib_ops.py","norm_id":"n711128ba5740e833","priority":0.7556,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["AC5 conditions deletion on ALL sites being migrated; a wrong denominator can leave a site migrated-but-uncounted or claim coverage of a non-existent site"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Replace 'EIGHTEEN ... eleven in _lib_ops.py ... eight NON-LLM' with 'SIXTEEN ... ten in _lib_ops.py (three LLM workflow ops plus seven NON-LLM bridge ops)', and update the Scope bullet ('migrate all eleven ... eight non-LLM') accordingly.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8889,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"contradicts_reality","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"medium","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Enumerate the test consumers of the deleted shadow symbols (tests/unit/test_single_definition_helpers.py, tests/unit/test_operation_snapshot.py, tests/interfaces/contracts/test_operation_snapshot_surfaces.py) in Scope and specify how each is updated or removed when emit_shadow_snapshot/_shadow/shadow_enabled/SHADOW_ENV are deleted.","cohort":["G1G2"],"criteria":["G1G2"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.1889,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["tests/unit/test_single_definition_helpers.py:88-89 asserts _shadow is defined exactly once and lines 57-58/72-73 monkeypatch _operation_config.emit_shadow_snapshot; line 111 asserts _lib_ops._shadow is _mcp_llm._shadow","tests/unit/test_operation_snapshot.py:30 imports emit_shadow_snapshot and lines 283/301/308 assert its swallow behavior","tests/interfaces/contracts/test_operation_snapshot_surfaces.py:95,156 reference emit_shadow_snapshot","Scope's Testing bullet lists only 'Focused LLM/provider/cache/fallback/workflow tests and cross-surface contract tests' plus the new parity file — it does not name these shadow-dependent unit/contract tests"],"finding":"AC5 deletes emit_shadow_snapshot, _shadow, shadow_enabled, and SHADOW_ENV, but existing test modules outside the artifact directory directly depend on these symbols and are not enumerated as consumers requiring update in Scope.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f7de0b026840f4adf","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria AC5 / Scope (Testing bullet only names new/focused suites generically)","norm_id":"na95dccdae1a61cca","priority":0.8889,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Deleting the four symbols per AC5 breaks import/assertion in test_operation_snapshot.py and the single-definition/identity assertions in test_single_definition_helpers.py, failing the default suite the plan requires to pass"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8889,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"omits_required_site","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Resolve resign_plan_review's classification: state whether it binds the LLM composer (and if so, why it should fail-fast on auth it never uses) or the auth-optional path, and add it to (or explicitly exempt it from) the parity artifact's compose-once assertion list.","cohort":["T8"],"criteria":["T8"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.1889,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan classification: the five _mcp_llm.py tools bind the new composer 'via the rebar.llm.review_code/verify_completion/review_plan/resign_plan_review/scan_epics_for_spec entry points'","AC3 section: the LLM composer 'does NOT inherit that swallow: LLMConfig.from_env()'s ConfigError/credential/provider-resolution failures propagate uncaught, so an LLM op with unresolvable auth fails before any external call'","Parity artifact compose-once list names 'review_code/verify_completion/review_plan/scan_epics_for_spec/run_workflow' — resign_plan_review is absent","Code: src/rebar/_mcp_llm.py sign_review docstring states it is 'NOT gated on REBAR_MCP_ALLOW_LLM (it makes no LLM call)'; it calls rebar.llm.resign_plan_review, a cheap re-persist from the sidecar with 'no LLM, no network'"],"finding":"resign_plan_review (the sign_review MCP tool) is classified as one of the five LLM sites bound to the new compose_and_bind_llm_config and therefore held to AC3 fail-fast on unresolvable auth/provider composition, yet the op makes no LLM call and needs no auth, and the parity artifact's compose-once list omits it — leaving the binding/fail-fast decision rule for this op unspecified and contradictory.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f578861c7dcf2e10d","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach 'Call-site classification' and 'Parity-verification artifact'; AC3","norm_id":"ndba369396ffd72b2","priority":0.8889,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An operator runs sign_review/resign_plan_review in an environment with no model API key to recover a transient sign failure; if the op inherits AC3 fail-fast auth resolution it errors before the (LLM-free) re-sign, regressing a currently-working recovery path","An executor implementing the binding cannot decide whether resign_plan_review should compose the LLM projection (and fail-fast) or take the general/no-auth path"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Since resign_plan_review makes no LLM call and needs no credentials, either bind it to the auth-optional general snapshot path (not AC3 fail-fast) or note that its LLM projection must not require resolvable auth; then reconcile the compose-once parity list to match the chosen contract.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8889,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"high","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Re-derive the `_shadow`/`emit_shadow_snapshot` call-site inventory from the symbol graph (find_referencing_symbols on `_shadow` and `emit_shadow_snapshot`, plus a string grep for both names) and correct the counts: `_lib_ops.py` has 10 physical `_shadow(...)` sites (3 workflow + 7 non-LLM, with bridge_preview/bridge_sync sharing the line-224 site in `_bridge_run`), giving a physical total of 16 (5 mcp + 10 lib_ops + 1 reconciler), not 18.","cohort":["project.symbol-reference-completeness"],"criteria":["project.symbol-reference-completeness"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.1444,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'emit_shadow_snapshot/_shadow ... has EIGHTEEN production call sites, not just five: five in _mcp_llm.py (LLM), eleven in _lib_ops.py (three LLM workflow ops ... plus eight NON-LLM bridge/reconciler-mapping ops), and one in _engine/rebar_reconciler/__main__.py'","src/rebar/_lib_ops.py has exactly 10 physical `_shadow(...)` calls (lines 58,76,86,102,110,129,150,224,264,289); line 224 `_shadow(f\"lib.bridge_{route}\")` inside `_bridge_run` is the sole site for BOTH bridge_preview (line 257) and bridge_sync (line 276)","5 (_mcp_llm) + 10 (_lib_ops) + 1 (reconciler) = 16 physical sites, not the 18 claimed nor the 17 the plan's own numbers sum to"],"finding":"The `_shadow`/`emit_shadow_snapshot` deletion inventory (AC5) overstates the `_lib_ops.py` call-site count: the plan asserts 'eleven in `_lib_ops.py`' (and 'eight NON-LLM ... eight `_shadow(...)` sites'), but only 10 physical `_shadow(...)` call sites exist (lines 58,76,86,102,110,129,150,224,264,289) — 3 workflow + 7 non-LLM. There is no eighth physical non-LLM site: `bridge_preview` and `bridge_sync` share the single `_shadow(f\"lib.bridge_{route}\")` at line 224 inside `_bridge_run`. The plan's own breakdown (5+11+1) sums to 17 while it claims EIGHTEEN; the verified physical total is 16 (5+10+1). The list conflates public ops (8) with patch sites (7), which is exactly the silent-miscount failure mode symbol-graph derivation guards against.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fe65ee8d09770341b","impact":0.85,"is_primary":null,"location":"Context/Problem: 'EIGHTEEN production call sites ... five in `_mcp_llm.py` ... eleven in `_lib_ops.py` ...' and Scope: 'migrate all eleven `_shadow(...)` sites: ... eight non-LLM bridge/reconciler-mapping ops'","norm_id":"ne70b4626d963173e","priority":0.7556,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A migrator following 'eleven `_shadow(...)` sites' in _lib_ops.py searches for an 11th physical site that does n